@startuml order-lifecycle
!include _common.iuml
title Order Lifecycle — State Model (SRS §5.3)

[*] --> Draft : customer initiates checkout

Draft --> PendingPayment : order placed,\nstock reserved
Draft --> Cancelled : customer abandons /\ncart expires

PendingPayment --> Paid : payment authorised\nand captured
PendingPayment --> PaymentFailed : gateway declines /\ntimeout
PendingPayment --> Cancelled : customer cancels

PaymentFailed --> PendingPayment : customer retries payment
PaymentFailed --> Cancelled : retry window elapses

Paid --> Processing : accepted by\nfulfilment
Paid --> Cancelled : cancelled before\npicking starts

Processing --> Packed : items picked and packed
Processing --> Cancelled : stock shortfall confirmed

Packed --> Shipping : handed to carrier
Shipping --> Delivered : carrier confirms delivery
Delivered --> Completed : return window closes
Delivered --> Returned : customer returns\nwithin return window

Cancelled --> Refunded : captured payment\nreversed
Returned --> Refunded : returned goods\nreceived and accepted

Completed --> [*]
Refunded --> [*]

state Draft #FBFAFF
state PendingPayment as "Pending Payment"
state PaymentFailed as "Payment Failed"

note right of Cancelled
  BR-ORD-01: only the transitions drawn here
  are legal. Any other transition must be
  rejected regardless of entry point (P5).
end note

note left of Paid
  BR-INV-02: reserved stock is committed on
  entry to Processing and released on entry
  to Cancelled — never both, never neither (P7).
end note
@enduml
